<section id="autoshield-full-pipeline-report"
 style="margin-top:22px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px;background:#fff">
 <h2 style="margin:0 0 6px">Complete AutoShield AI Pipeline Report</h2>
 <p style="color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 18px">
 Incident INC-001 · Recorded outputs and evaluation results
 </p>

 <div class="report-row"><span>1. Evidence ingestion</span>
 <b>50 normalized events and 50 timeline events recorded. Evidence sources include proxy and application logs, container metadata, network captures and configuration artifacts.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>2. Graph and GNN</span>
 <b>30 graph nodes and 24 edges. Held-out test n=12: precision 1.000, recall 0.7778, F1 0.875, accuracy 0.8333. Results are preliminary and use scenario-intent labels.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>3. Incident reconstruction</span>
 <b>Two SQL-injection-shaped requests were observed about 1 ms apart. Their relationship remains a candidate correlation. Database access and exfiltration were not independently verified.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>4. LLM narrative</span>
 <b>Narrative synthesis output is recorded. Validation checks evidence references and limits unsupported root-cause confirmation; this does not prove every generated statement is true.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>5. Security knowledge / RAG</span>
 <b>FTS5 BM25 retrieval; 10 unique CAPEC/CWE references recorded for the example incident. Retrieved material supports analysis and recommendations, not proof of exploitation.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>6. Remediation planning</span>
 <b>Remediation recommendations are advisory. A recommendation alone does not establish that a change was applied or that it was effective.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>7. Penetration testing / validation</span>
 <b>Controlled validation outcome is not established in this report. The recorded scenario observed Nginx-to-API forwarding and an HTTP response; downstream database activity remains unverified.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>8. Judge Agent</span>
 <b>Pending recorded decision. No PASS/FAIL outcome is claimed without a supporting execution artifact.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>9. SHAP explainability</span>
 <b>For scenario_011, raw GCN edge logit ≈ 40.1342 and baseline ≈ −2.9315. Largest positive contributions include HTTP feature IDs 21, 18 and 6. Reconstruction error ≈ 7.11 × 10⁻¹⁵. The logit is not a calibrated probability.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>10. Bayesian Neural Network</span>
 <b>500 posterior samples; 12 held-out test edges. Accuracy 0.8333, precision 1.000, recall 0.7778, F1 0.875, Brier score 0.0712 and MAE 0.2173. This predicts attack-edge-label proxy scores, not validated post-remediation residual risk.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>11. BNN limitations</span>
 <b>The held-out set is small (n=12). Predictive intervals and prototype risk bands are not empirically calibrated for operational residual-risk decisions.</b></div>

 <div class="report-row"><span>Overall status</span>
 <b>Evidence analysis, graph/GNN evaluation, narrative synthesis, RAG retrieval, SHAP and BNN outputs are documented. Remediation effectiveness, controlled post-remediation validation and Judge decisions must be supported by execution evidence before being marked successful.</b></div>
</section>
